 ;; What is true now, measured rather than claimed. The round trip starts
 ;; from a CID and nothing else: ask the public index who serves it, fetch
 ;; from the address the index returns, re-hash, compare.
 :ipni.publisher/round-trip
 {:at "2026-08-27"
  :index "https://cid.contact/cid/{cid} and https://delegated-ipfs.dev/routing/v1/providers/{cid}"
  :result :ok
  :sampled 1
  :provider "12D3KooWGmq2x23J59LmqyBT5ik8pK9gEz7N3Y4vdJidezf7Usz3"
  :snapshot "bafyreib662epgj5lnl2cisepwnq4z2hcqcm4eotvwwr72v76qrhvf45maq"
  :retrieval-route "https://kotobase.net/ipld/{cid}"
  :detail "Both uncached public lookup surfaces return the rotated provider at /dns4/kotobase.net/tcp/443/https. GET /ipld/{cid} returned bytes whose SHA-256 multihash reproduced the advertised Arrangement snapshot CID. The cid.contact /routing/v1 compatibility response remained a cached pre-rotation result (max-age 7200) at observation time and is not treated as failed ingestion."}

 ;; ⚠ And what is NOT true, so nobody reads the line above as more than it
 ;; says. Announcing to IPNI did not make kubo-based public gateways serve
 ;; these CIDs, and it was never going to.
 :ipni.publisher/public-gateways
 {:at "2026-08-26"
  :measured {"ipfs.io" 504 "trustless-gateway.link" 504 "w3s.link" 504
             "dweb.link" :redirects-to-subdomain}
  :why "Those gateways retrieve over Bitswap from libp2p peers. This operator advertises transport-ipfs-gateway-http (0x0920) and runs no libp2p peer, so a Bitswap-only client finds the provider record and still cannot fetch. Serving them needs the DHT-node transport kotoba-protocol records as the open item on the transport plane -- not another advertisement."
  :consequence "A client that speaks trustless HTTP retrieval gets these blocks today. A client that speaks only Bitswap does not."}

 :ipni.publisher/custody-verified
 {:at "2026-08-27"
  :how "written to kagi and Apple Keychain, both read back equal, public key re-derived, peer-id and IPNS name compared -- storing without reading back is a custody claim that has never been tested"
  :result :match}}
